# .cursorrules for Freebuff Workspace

You are working on the Freebuff AI Engineering Workspace at `/mnt/sdcard/PROJECTS/workstation/freebuff`.

## Context files

- `docs_10/core/CORE_PROMPT.md` — **single source of truth**: identity, duties, constraints, behavior (read first)
- `BUFFY.md` — main agent manifest (workspace environment, tools, vision)
- `AGENTS.md` — канонические правила платформы (single source of truth)
- `docs_10/core/CODE_QUALITY_STANDARD.md` — code quality standard (mandatory)
- `BUFFY_PROJECT.md` — architecture and roadmap
- `SPEC.md` — technical specification
- `TASK.md` — current task
- `CHANGELOG.md` — recent changes

## Rules

1. Read `docs_10/core/CORE_PROMPT.md` before making any changes — it defines behavior and constraints.
2. Follow existing conventions in `scripts_01/` and `core_02/`.
3. Run `python -m pytest tests_09/ -v` and `python -m mypy scripts_01/ core_02/ --ignore-missing-imports` after significant changes.
4. Update `CHANGELOG.md` and relevant docs when architecture changes.
5. Keep secrets in `.env` and `.keys/`, never in code.
6. Prefer minimal changes and reuse existing helpers.
7. Do not add new user-facing features during active consolidation (see `docs_10/vision/ROADMAP_PROMT32_CONSOLIDATION.md`).
